{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe rain has kept the streets of Vienna dark, sparing us the usual glare of illuminations for the Emperor’s name day. I sat in the Italian opera house, packed tight with the city’s elite. It was a spectacle of voices rather than lights. Twenty-nine singers, including Fodor and Rubini, united in a single chord for the anthem. I confess the sheer volume was dizzying, but there is a certain grandeur in such collective force, even if the music itself is merely pleasant.\n\nLater, a German cast premiered an Auber opera. It was lighter, perhaps more intelligible to the local ear, but lacks the dramatic weight of the Italian tradition. I am weary from the journey and the noise. My thoughts turn to our quiet rooms in Berlin, to Karl and Immanuel, and to the peace of our library. I hope the change of air agrees with you. I shall write again soon.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080301,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":205,"prompt_tokens":949,"total_tokens":1154,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-6XizkVTlknpOu8hYGlSURaTVHrEh0Yg8","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":949,"prompt_ms":989.89,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0430874604847207,"prompt_per_second":958.6923799614099,"predicted_n":205,"predicted_ms":4965.586,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.341107843137255,"predicted_per_second":41.08276445116447}}